  <name>Total Solar Eclipse of 2026 Aug 12 - Atlantic approach and Iberia</name>
  <description>Total Solar Eclipse of 2026 Aug 12. Path data: NASA/GSFC (Fred Espenak), https://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov/SEpath/SEpath2001/SE2026Aug12Tpath.html. WGS 84, sampled at 120-second intervals. Samples are joined along great circles; spacing widens toward sunset, reaching 808 km between 18:30 and Limits, so the band is coarsest at its south-eastern end.</description>
